.Dd September 28, 2026
.Dt EDIAGCBOR 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ediagcbor
.Nd emergency diagnostic converter between CBOR and EDN
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl e | Fl d
.Op Fl i Ar input
.Op Fl o Ar output
.Op Ar file
.Op options
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Bf -emphasis
Warning: This is an AI-generated version and is expected to be reviewed
and massively refactored.
It is not intended for inclusion in a base system yet.
You will know it is ready when this manual page is complete.
.Ef
.Pp
.Nm
converts between binary Concise Binary Object Representation
.Pq CBOR, RFC 8949
and CBOR Extended Diagnostic Notation
.Pq EDN .
It targets emergency / single-user recovery situations
— for example when file systems with packages are unavailable and only a
read-only root file system remains.
In all other cases, prefer fuller EDN implementations written in
higher-level languages.
.Pp
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl e , Fl -encode
Read EDN, write CBOR.
.It Fl d , Fl -decode
Read CBOR, write pretty-printed EDN, recovering known literals where possible
.Pq e.g. tag 52/54 as Ic IP'...' , tag 1 as Ic DT'...' .
ASCII-printable byte strings are written as
.Ic '...'
instead of
.Ic h'' .
.It Fl i Ar path
Input file (binary for decode, text for encode).
.It Fl o Ar path
Output file (default: standard output).
.El
.Pp
If neither
.Fl e
nor
.Fl d
is given, the mode is guessed from the input path:
names ending in
.Dq cbor
select decode; names ending in
.Dq dn
.Pq e.g. Ic .edn , Ic .cedn
select encode.
Otherwise
.Pq stdin or unrecognized suffix
encode is the default.
.Ss Brief CBOR primer
CBOR
.Pq RFC 8949
is a binary data format with major types: unsigned/negative integers,
byte strings, text strings, arrays, maps, tags, and simple values / floats.
Tags attach semantics to a nested item (epoch time is tag 1; IPv4/IPv6
addresses and prefixes use tags 52 and 54 per RFC 9164).
.Ss Brief EDN primer
EDN is a human-readable notation for CBOR items
.Pq draft-ietf-cbor-edn-literals .
Examples:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
true, 42, "text", h'a1b2', [1, 2], {"a": 1}
1(1690000000)          # tag
DT'2023-07-22T00:26:40Z'
IP'192.0.2.1'
IP'2001:db8::/32'
.Ed
.Pp
Application-extension literals
.Pq Ic dt'' , Ic IP'' , Ic h'' , ...
decode to ordinary CBOR; on
.Fl d ,
.Nm
tries to print the convenient form again.
.Ss Ingest options
Default EDN parsing follows the CBOR WG chairs' post-27 removals.
Legacy draft \-27 behaviour is restored with:
.Fl -ellipsis ,
.Fl -tag999 ,
.Fl -c-comments ,
.Fl -eol-slash-comments ,
.Fl -legacy-numbers ,
.Fl -indicator-suffix ,
.Fl -raw-delim-max Ns = Ns Ar N .
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
ediagcbor -e -i msg.edn -o msg.cbor
ediagcbor -d dump.cbor
ediagcbor packet.cbor          # guesses -d
ediagcbor note.edn             # guesses -e
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
RFC 8949, RFC 9164,
.Lk https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-cbor-edn-literals/
